bug_report:
Designated initializer doesn't support direct-initialization
This currently fails to compile on trunk:

struct X {
    explicit X() { }
};

struct Aggr {
    X x;
};

Aggr f() {
    return Aggr{.x{}};
}

source>: In function 'Aggr f()':
<source>:10:21: error: converting to 'X' from initializer list would use explicit constructor 'X::X()'
   10 |     return Aggr{.x{}};
      |                     ^
Compiler returned: 1

But it's intended to work (this is CWG 2359).
